# **`npm ci` fails without this, so a fresh clone cannot install the client.**
#
# `eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y` 6.10.2 peers on eslint `^9` and has published
# nothing since October 2024, so npm refuses the tree against eslint 10. There
# is no successor to move to -- it is the only implementation of these checks,
# and `ui/eslint.config.js` carries the argument for keeping it.
#
# **It weakens every future peer check, which is the cost.** npm will accept
# any conflicting peer here, not only this one -- so `ui/src/eslintPeers.test.ts`
# fails the day the plugin gains an eslint 10 range, which is the reminder to
# delete this file.
#
# **npm's silence is therefore not evidence.** With this set, an ERESOLVE that
# would have named a real conflict never prints. A peer question is answered by
# `npm ls <package>` reporting one deduped copy, never by an install that said
# nothing.
#
# **At the root since the move to workspaces, and that widened it.** npm reads
# this file from the directory it installs in, and a workspace install runs
# here -- a copy left in `ui/` would be read by nobody and the install would
# fail with ERESOLVE. So the weakening now covers `server/` too, which had no
# peer conflicts of its own to lose.
legacy-peer-deps=true
